# Posts and pages

Posts are Markdown files in `src/posts/`. Standalone pages (about, contact, projects) are Markdown in `src/pages/` and are loaded by their matching route. Do not add a CMS, a content database, or a second content folder.

The filename is the slug. `getPosts()` in `src/lib/posts.ts` only lists a post when `published` is true.

Post frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: Post title
description: One or two sentences for the listing and meta description.
date: 'YYYY-MM-DD'
categories:
  - sveltekit
published: true
---
```

- Keep `date` as a quoted `YYYY-MM-DD` string.
- Use lowercase category slugs already used on the site (`sveltekit`, `wordpress`, `hosting`, `review`) unless a new category is clearly needed.
- Write public copy in British English.
- Link to posts as `/${slug}/`.
